{"name":"Toasted Chestnut","hex":"#a7775b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toasted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cooked by toasting.","Very hot."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of toast"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toasted"},{"term":"chestnut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible nut (technically a fruit) of the Spanish chestnut or sweet chestnut tree (Castanea sativa); also (chiefly preceded by a descriptive word), a nut from a related shrub or tree; or a similar nut from an unrelated plant.","In full chestnut tree: the shrub or tree that bears this nut, the Spanish chestnut or sweet chestnut (Castanea sativa); also (chiefly preceded by a descriptive word), a shrub or tree of the genus Castanea."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep reddish-brown colour, like that of a chestnut fruit (noun sense 1)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chestnut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toast (food)","blocks":[{"text":"Toast is sliced bread that has been browned by radiant heat. The browning is the result of a Maillard reaction altering the flavor of the bread and making it crispier in texture. The firm surface is easier to spread toppings on and the warmth can help spreads such as butter reach their melting point. Toasting is a common method of making stale bread more palatable. Bread is commonly toasted using devices specifically designed for such, e.g., a toaster or a toaster oven. Toast may contain more acrylamide, caused by the browning process, which is suspected to be a carcinogen. However, claims that acrylamide in burnt food causes cancer have not been proven."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Toast-3.jpg/330px-Toast-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toast_(food)","wikidata":"Q6128"},{"title":"Chestnut","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnuts are the deciduous trees and shrubs in the genus Castanea, in the beech family Fagaceae. The name also refers to the edible nuts they produce. They are native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Ch%C3%A2taignier_120807_1.jpg/330px-Ch%C3%A2taignier_120807_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut","wikidata":"Q129324"},{"title":"Chestnut (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnut or castaneous is a colour, a medium reddish shade of brown, and is named after the nut of the chestnut tree. An alternate name for the colour is badious."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut_(color)","wikidata":"Q2040833"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Toaster.jpg/500px-Toaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Toaster.jpg/1280px-Toaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Toaster.jpg/500px-Toaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A classic two-slot toaster","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AToaster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg/500px-Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg/1280px-Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg/500px-Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Left: Toast with butter and Vegemite. R